# Estimation and smoothing

This branch reconstructs hidden state from noisy observations. `lqe` designs a steady-state estimator gain. `kalman` performs forward recursive filtering for a discrete state-space model, while `smooth` adds a backward pass that conditions earlier state estimates on later observations.

## Data Contract

Observations end in `[time, outputs]`; optional known inputs end in `[time, inputs]`. Leading batch axes broadcast. Missing observation lanes may be represented by non-finite values and are omitted through the information-form update rather than contaminating an entire trajectory.

## Practical Examples

The examples run a forward filter, compare filtered and smoothed trajectories, and demonstrate estimator validation.

